  "Number": 7,
  "Question": "If the digit \\(1\\) is placed after a two digit number whose tens’ digit is \\(t,\\) and units’ digit is \\(u,\\) the new number is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(10t+u+1\\)",
    "B": "\\(100t+10u+1\\)",
    "C": "\\(1000t+10u+1\\)",
    "D": "\\(t+u+1\\)",
    "E": "None of these answers"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Placing \\(1\\) after the original number shifts each original digit one place to the left. The digit \\(t\\) is now in the hundreds place, \\(u\\) is in the tens place, and \\(1\\) is in the units place. Therefore the new number is\n\\[\n\\boxed{100t+10u+1},\n\\]\nwhich is choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
